{% doc %}
  The shipping estimator, shared by the cart page and the cart drawer.

  One copy, because two would drift — and a customer who gets one estimate in the
  drawer and a different one on the cart page has been given a reason not to
  trust either.

  Rates come from Shopify's own endpoint. The theme neither computes nor caches
  them, so the estimate is the same number checkout will use, and a merchant
  changing a shipping profile sees the change immediately.

  ## The ids are namespaced

  The drawer and the cart page can both be in the document at once, and duplicate
  `id` attributes break every `<label for>` on the page — the browser binds each
  label to whichever element it finds first, so clicking one form's label focuses
  the other form's field.

  Province lists come from Shopify's `country_option_tags`, read from the
  selected option rather than fetched. A theme shipping its own list of provinces
  would be wrong somewhere in the world within a year.

  @param {string} id - Unique per instance, e.g. 'drawer' or 'page'
  @param {boolean} [heading] - Render the title. Default true

  @example
    {% render 'shipping-calculator', id: 'drawer' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign instance = id | default: 'page'
  assign show_heading = heading
  if heading == nil
    assign show_heading = true
  endif
-%}

<shipping-calculator class="shipping-calculator">
  {%- if show_heading -%}
    <h2 class="shipping-calculator__title">{{ 'cart.shipping_calculator.title' | t }}</h2>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="shipping-calculator__fields">
    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="ShippingCountry-{{ instance }}">{{ 'cart.shipping_calculator.country' | t }}</label>
      <select id="ShippingCountry-{{ instance }}" data-ref="country" name="country">
        {{ country_option_tags }}
      </select>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Hidden until a country with provinces is chosen. An empty dropdown reads as
      a required field a customer cannot fill.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="form-field" data-province-wrapper hidden>
      <label for="ShippingProvince-{{ instance }}">{{ 'cart.shipping_calculator.province' | t }}</label>
      <select id="ShippingProvince-{{ instance }}" data-ref="province" name="province" disabled></select>
    </div>

    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="ShippingZip-{{ instance }}">{{ 'cart.shipping_calculator.zip' | t }}</label>
      <input
        id="ShippingZip-{{ instance }}"
        data-ref="zip"
        name="zip"
        autocomplete="postal-code"
        autocapitalize="characters"
      >
    </div>
  </div>

  <button type="button" class="button button--secondary" data-ref="submit">
    {{ 'cart.shipping_calculator.calculate' | t }}
  </button>

  <div class="shipping-calculator__results" data-ref="results" role="status"></div>
</shipping-calculator>
